{
 "_comment": "Popular package names used by the supply-chain scanner (aegis/scanners/supplychain.py). 'npm' and 'pypi' hold the most-downloaded packages: they are never flagged as typosquats and they are the names other packages are compared against (edit distance 1, look-alike characters, separator changes). 'npm_legit' and 'pypi_legit' hold other well-known packages, including legitimate near-name packages (preact, uid, ext, pyaml, cattrs ...), that must never be flagged as typosquats and whose install scripts are trusted. 'npm_scopes' are popular npm scopes used for scope look-alike checks. PyPI names are PEP 503 normalised (lower case, runs of - _ . become -).",
 "_sources": [
  "PyPI: hugovk/top-pypi-packages top-15000 list https://hugovk.github.io/top-pypi-packages/top-pypi-packages.min.json (last_update 2026-10-01); look-alike names ranked below 7000 are treated as legitimate",
  "npm: weekly download counts from https://api.npmjs.org/downloads/point/last-week (2026-10-06 to 2026-10-12) for a hand-picked candidate list (targets: >= 5,000,000 weekly); look-alike names with >= 50,000 weekly downloads are treated as legitimate"
 ],
